.TH "PVSECRET-CREATE-ASSOCIATION" "1" "2026-08-11" "s390-tools" "UV\-Secret Manual"
.nh
.ad l
.SH "NAME"
pvsecret-create-association \- Create an association secret
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.fam C
\fBpvsecret\fR \fBcreate\fR \fBassociation\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME>
.fam C
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Use an association secret to connect a trusted I/O device to a guest. The
\fBpvapconfig\fR tool provides more information about association secrets.
.SH "OPTIONS"
<NAME>
.RS 4
String that identifies the new secret.

The actual secret is set with \fB\-\-input\-secret\fR. The name is saved in
`NAME.yaml` with white\-spaces mapped to `_`.
.RE
.PP
\-\-stdout
.RS 4
Print the hashed name to stdout.

The hashed name is not written to `NAME.yaml`
.RE
.PP
\-\-input\-secret <SECRET\-FILE>
.RS 4
Path from which to read the plaintext secret. Uses a random secret if not
specified.
.RE
.PP
\-\-output\-secret <SECRET\-FILE>
.RS 4
Save the generated secret as plaintext in SECRET\-FILE.

The generated secret can be used to generate add\-secret requests for a
different guest with the same secret using \fB\-\-input\-secret\fR. Destroy the
secret when it is not used anymore.
.RE
.PP
\-h, \-\-help
.RS 4
Print help (see a summary with \fB\-h\fR).
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBpvsecret\fR(1), \fBpvsecret\-create\fR(1)